<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="UTF-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><meta name="theme-color" content="#142d4c"><meta name="description" content="Explore assistance programs available in California."><title>California Assistance Programs — American Aid Network</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/site.css"></head><body><?php require __DIR__ . "/../../includes/site-header.php"; ?><main><section class="state-page"><div class="wrap"><div class="breadcrumbs"><a href="/">Home</a><span>›</span><a href="/help/">Browse Programs</a><span>›</span><b>California</b></div><div class="state-intro"><div><h1>Assistance Programs in California</h1><p>9 programs, grouped by what you need help with. Each includes clear application guidance.</p></div><div><a class="button primary" href="/find/">Find my programs <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><small>Free · Private · Takes under 2 minutes</small></div></div><section class="program-group"><h2>Utility Bill Help</h2><div class="directory-cards"><article><h3>CARE / FERA (Utility Bill Discounts)</h3><p>30-35% discount on electricity and 20% on gas bills from PG&amp;E, SCE, SoCalGas, and SDG&amp;E for income-qualified households. Enrollment is a short form with your utility.</p><div><a href="/programs/care-fera-utility-bill-discounts/">How to apply <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a href="/programs/care-fera-utility-bill-discounts/">Program details <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></article><article><h3>California LIHEAP (Energy Assistance)</h3><p>Help paying energy bills and shutoff emergencies, delivered through local community action agencies.</p><div><a href="/programs/california-liheap-energy-assistance/">How to apply <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a href="/programs/california-liheap-energy-assistance/">Program details <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></article></div><a class="group-cta" href="/find/">Check what you qualify for <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></section><section class="program-group"><h2>Debt &amp; Credit Help</h2><div class="directory-cards"><article><h3>CalEITC + Young Child Tax Credit</h3><p>Cash-back state tax credits worth hundreds to thousands of dollars for low-income workers — even if you owe no taxes. Free tax prep available.</p><div><a href="/programs/caleitc-young-child-tax-credit/">How to apply <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a href="/programs/caleitc-young-child-tax-credit/">Program details <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></article></div><a class="group-cta" href="/find/">Check what you qualify for <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></section><section class="program-group"><h2>Food Assistance</h2><div class="directory-cards"><article><h3>CalFresh (California SNAP)</h3><p>California&#39;s food benefits program — monthly money on an EBT card for groceries. Apply through BenefitsCal, the state&#39;s official benefits site, or call 1-877-847-3663. (GetCalFresh no longer takes applications.)</p><div><a href="/programs/calfresh-california-snap/">How to apply <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a href="/programs/calfresh-california-snap/">Program details <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></article></div><a class="group-cta" href="/find/">Check what you qualify for <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></section><section class="program-group"><h2>Cash Assistance &amp; Benefits</h2><div class="directory-cards"><article><h3>CalWORKs (Cash Aid for Families)</h3><p>Monthly cash assistance plus job services and child care for California families with children in need.</p><div><a href="/programs/calworks-cash-aid-for-families/">How to apply <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a href="/programs/calworks-cash-aid-for-families/">Program details <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></article><article><h3>EDD Unemployment &amp; Disability Insurance</h3><p>Unemployment benefits if you lost work, State Disability Insurance if you can&#39;t work due to illness/injury, and Paid Family Leave.</p><div><a href="/programs/edd-unemployment-and-disability-insurance/">How to apply <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a href="/programs/edd-unemployment-and-disability-insurance/">Program details <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></article></div><a class="group-cta" href="/find/">Check what you qualify for <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></section><section class="program-group"><h2>Rent &amp; Housing Assistance</h2><div class="directory-cards"><article><h3>California Courts Self-Help (Eviction)</h3><p>Official guides on responding to an eviction notice in California — you typically have only 5 business days to respond to a court summons. Free self-help centers at every courthouse.</p><div><a href="/programs/california-courts-self-help-eviction/">How to apply <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a href="/programs/california-courts-self-help-eviction/">Program details <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></article></div><a class="group-cta" href="/find/">Check what you qualify for <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></section><section class="program-group"><h2>Free &amp; Low-Cost Healthcare</h2><div class="directory-cards"><article><h3>Covered California</h3><p>California&#39;s health insurance marketplace with income-based subsidies if you earn too much for Medi-Cal.</p><div><a href="/programs/covered-california/">How to apply <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a href="/programs/covered-california/">Program details <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></article><article><h3>Medi-Cal (California Medicaid)</h3><p>Free or low-cost health coverage for low-income Californians — doctor visits, prescriptions, mental health, and dental for most members.</p><div><a href="/programs/medi-cal-california-medicaid/">How to apply <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a href="/programs/medi-cal-california-medicaid/">Program details <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></article></div></section></div></section></main><footer><div class="wrap footer-grid"><div><a class="brand" href="/" aria-label="American Aid Network home"><span class="brand-mark" aria-hidden="true"><span>★</span><i></i><i></i><i></i></span><span>AMERICAN <b>AID</b><small>NETWORK</small></span></a><p>Clear, reliable guidance to assistance programs across America.</p><div class="verified">✓ Information from trusted sources</div></div><div><h4>FIND SUPPORT</h4><a href="/find/">Find help near me</a><a href="/help/">Browse by state</a><a href="/programs/">Program guides</a><a href="/#how-it-works">How it works</a></div><div><h4>ABOUT</h4><a href="/about/">Our mission</a><a href="/legal/contact/">Contact us</a><a href="/legal/privacy/">Privacy policy</a><a href="/legal/terms/">Terms of use</a></div></div><div class="wrap disclaimer">American Aid Network is an independent informational resource. We are not a government agency and do not administer benefit programs. Program details change; always confirm requirements with the official provider.<span>© 2026 American Aid Network</span></div></footer><script src="/assets/site.js" defer></script></body></html>